<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nepali Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nepali Congress is a social democratic political party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, formed in 1950 from earlier anti-Rana movements. With King Tribhuvan and Indian backing it helped end the rule of the Rana prime ministers in 1951, and its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/b-p-koirala">B. P. Koirala</a> became the first elected prime minister in 1959. Banned under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panchayat">Panchayat</a> system from 1960, it led the 1990 People's Movement and has headed many governments since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nepali-congress.jpg" alt="Nepali Congress" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Connormah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nepali_Congress_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
